TI  - Generalizability of electrocardiographic artificial intelligence.
LID - 10.1038/s44325-025-00078-2 [doi]
LID - 38
AB  - Electrocardiographic artificial intelligence (ECG-AI) uses AI-based algorithms to 
      analyze ECGs. Recent literature has revealed the untapped potential of ECG beyond 
      traditional diagnostics. ECG-AI is now used not only to detect arrhythmias but 
      also to assess risk and identify both cardiovascular and non-cardiovascular 
      conditions. This perspective article summarizes evidence from published 
      literature to support the conclusion that ECG-AI models are highly generalizable 
      and have the potential to revolutionize healthcare.
