OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20251203
LR  - 20251203
IS  - 2694-0604 (Electronic)
IS  - 2375-7477 (Linking)
VI  - 2025
DP  - 2025 Jul
TI  - Cardiorespiratory Correlation Coefficient Matrices for CNN-Based Sleep Apnea 
      Detection.
PG  - 1-6
LID - 10.1109/EMBC58623.2025.11254655 [doi]
AB  - Sleep apnea is a disorder characterized by repetitive temporary cessation of 
      breath, with significant health implications if untreated, thus requiring 
      efficient and accurate identification methods. This paper proposes a novel 
      CNN-based approach for apnea detection from physiological signals: ECG, heart 
      rate, SpO₂, and respiratory signals. The novelty of this work consists in the 
      employment of physiological signal correlation coefficient matrices to represent 
      apnea manifestations. For classification, we employ a pre-trained ResNet-50 model 
      with transfer learning and apply data augmentation to enhance model 
      generalization. Matlab simulation results demonstrate high classification 
      performance, validating the proposed method for sleep apnea detection.Clinical 
      Relevance- This demonstrated the potential of AI-based physiological signal 
      correlation analysis for decision support system in sleep apnea diagnosis.
