PMID- 41336812
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20251203
LR  - 20251203
IS  - 2694-0604 (Electronic)
IS  - 2375-7477 (Linking)
VI  - 2025
DP  - 2025 Jul
TI  - Phase Space Reconstruction and Ensemble Voting to Localize Arrhythmogenic Zones 
      of the Ventricles.
PG  - 1-7
LID - 10.1109/EMBC58623.2025.11251549 [doi]
AB  - Premature ventricular contraction (PVC) and ventricular tachycardia (VT) are two 
      types of cardiac rhythm irregularities originating from the lower chambers of the 
      heart. In severe cases, these arrhythmias could lead to sudden cardiac arrest. 
      For patients unresponsive to pharmacological treatments, catheter ablation 
      becomes a necessary intervention. Precise localization of arrhythmia origins 
      significantly improves the surgical success rates, reduces procedure time and 
      minimizes complications. This study introduces an electrocardiogram (ECG) 
      analysis framework to predict ventricular arrhythmia origin zones. The framework 
      employs phase space reconstruction to map ECG signals into higher-dimensional 
      spaces, followed by a machine learning ensemble voting mechanism to identify 
      arrhythmogenic ventricular locations. This approach aims to enhance the precision 
      and efficiency of ventricular arrhythmia localization, contributing to improved 
      clinical outcomes.
