TI  - A MATLAB Algorithm to Automatically Estimate the QT Interval and Other ECG 
      Parameters and Validation Using a Machine Learning Approach in Congenital Long-QT 
      Syndrome.
PG  - 1470-1481
LID - 10.1007/s12265-025-10693-0 [doi]
AB  - Myocardial repolarization and QT duration are crucial markers for diagnosis and 
      monitoring of congenital long QT syndrome (LQTS). Here we present a novel 
      algorithm to automatically estimate the QT interval based on Lepeschkin's tangent 
      method, as well as parameters underlying T-wave morphology in digital 
      electrocardiograms (ECGs) of 466 patients with LQTS. The algorithm's performance 
      was validated using ECG data from 40 healthy controls. The results were compared 
      against expert measurement of the QT interval, as well as against the results of 
      the ECG device MUSE™ system. Applying an optimizable Support Vector Machine 
      classifier on the algorithm's outcomes achieved an accuracy of 78.1% and area 
      under the curve of 0.85 in classifying LQTS patients with a prolonged QTc 
      interval (upon QT_GS) from those with a normal QTc interval. The presented 
      MATLAB®-based algorithm offers a transparent and reproducible approach to 
      automatic QT interval estimation and QTc calculation in LQTS patients, 
      potentially improving automatized screening, diagnostic precision and patient 
      management.
