PMC - PMC12273486
OAB - An individual’s sex is typically classified as male or female at birth based on 
      the presence of either a penis or a clitoris. However, there are many common 
      features of male and female individuals at the metabolic and cellular levels. 
      These commonalities are neglected in disease risk prediction models when an 
      individual is labeled as male or female. This study proposes a novel, nonbinary 
      representation of sex to be used in disease risk prediction models. Our novel 
      nonbinary variable is derived via artificial intelligence applied to 
      electrocardiographic data. It predicts all-cause mortality, heart failure, and 
      kidney failure better than a binary sex variable.
