TI  - Challenging Black-Box Models: Interpretable Explanations for ECG Classification.
PG  - 587-588
LID - 10.3233/SHTI250405 [doi]
AB  - Deep learning methods achieve high performance, while often lacking 
      explainability, hindering application in the field. We propose the use of a 
      logistic regression classifier based on temporal aligned Electrocardiograms, and 
      the utilisation of interpretable feature importance. This work suggests that 
      non-deep learning based classifiers achieve comparable performance, and introduce 
      new opportunities to on-the-fly counterfactual explanations. The code, pretrained 
      model, and extracted kernels are available under github.com/imi-ms/rlign.
