TI  - Unobtrusive Bed Monitor State of the Art.
LID - 10.3390/s25061879 [doi]
LID - 1879
AB  - On average, people spend more than a quarter of their day in bed. If 
      physiological information could be collected automatically while we sleep, it 
      would be effective not only for health management but also for disease 
      prevention. Unobtrusive bed monitoring devices have been developed over the past 
      30 years or so to detect physiological information without awareness, and this 
      method attracted attention again in the 2020s, with the proliferation of deep 
      learning, AI, and IoT. This section describes the current state of the art.
