TI  - Harnessing Vision Transformer Insights for Advanced Electrocardiogram 
      Classification.
PG  - 1-4
LID - 10.1109/EMBC53108.2024.10782430 [doi]
AB  - In the domain of cardiac health monitoring, the precise analysis of ECG data is 
      paramount, especially in resource-constrained settings. Traditional bedside 
      monitoring systems, while effective, pose challenges in terms of cost and 
      accessibility. As a transformative solution, this study introduces a pioneering 
      approach to ECG data classification through the use of wearable electrocardiogram 
      (ECG) sensors, coupled with advanced Vision Transformer models. The primary 
      challenge in conventional ECG signal analysis lies in its time-consuming nature 
      and the limited capability of convolutional neural networks (CNNs) to capture the 
      global context, owing to their fixed-sized kernel filters. To address these 
      challenges, we propose a Vision Transformer architecture that classifying ECG 
      data by transforming one-dimensional ECG signals into a more comprehensive form. 
      We employ three state-of-the-art time series to imaging techniques: Markov 
      Transition Fields (MTF), Recurrence Plots (RP), and Gramian Angular Fields (GAF). 
      These techniques convert one-dimensional ECG signals into three-channel images, 
      optimizing them for Vision Transformer analysis. Utilizing comprehensive dataset 
      of ECG5000, our model demonstrates unparalleled performance in classifying ECG 
      data and it outstrips current state-of-the-art methods in various metrics, 
      delivering exceptional results.Clinical relevance-This advancement not only marks 
      a significant leap in the field of medical diagnostics, but also promises a more 
      accessible and efficient healthcare solution for resource-constrained 
      environments.
