TI  - MrSeNet: Electrocardiogram signal denoising based on multi-resolution residual 
      attention network.
PG  - 153858
LID - S0022-0736(24)00328-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jelectrocard.2024.153858 [doi]
AB  - Electrocardiography (ECG) is a widely used, non-invasive, and cost-effective 
      diagnostic method that plays a crucial role in the early detection and management 
      of cardiac conditions. However, the ECG signal is easily disrupted by various 
      noise signals in the real world, leading to a decrease in signal quality and 
      potentially compromising accurate clinical interpretation. With the goal of 
      reducing noise in ECG signals, this research proposes an end-to-end 
      multi-resolution deep learning network with attention mechanism, namely the 
      MrSeNet to perform effective denoising of ECG data. Our MrSeNet fuses features at 
      different scales for effective denoising with the squeeze-and-excitation module 
      to enhance the features of the ECG signal channel. CPSC2018 database and the 
      MIT-BIH database were used to verify the validity of the model by adding 
      different intensity noises based on NSTDB. Using Pearson correlation coefficient, 
      signal-to-noise ratio, and root mean square error performance evaluation model, 
      the experimental results show that MrSeNet performs better than the traditional 
      method, the model can achieve a good denoising effect to different degrees of 
      noise signal data, and has a good future application prospect.
