OAB - Sudden cardiac death (SCD) occurs when there are problems with the electrical 
      activity within the heart. It is a common cause of death throughout the world so 
      it would be beneficial to be able to easily identify individuals that are at high 
      risk of SCD. Electrocardiograms are a cheap and widely available way to measure 
      electrical activity in the heart. We developed a computational method that can 
      use electrocardiograms to determine whether a person is at increased risk of 
      having a SCD. Our computational method could allow clinicians to screen large 
      numbers of people and identify those at a higher risk of SCD. This could enable 
      regular monitoring of these people and might enable SCDs to be prevented in some 
      individuals.
